Binance investigates a possible security breach

@binance says its security teams are looking into reports of a potential security issue and that user funds are “completely safe.” The exchange has not confirmed a hack, says it will share updates only through official channels, and warns users to ignore unofficial links and messages.

Tether CEO @paoloardoino said the company has frozen more than $1.56B in $USDT tied to the potential hack, while Circle CEO @jerallaire said it froze more than $800M in $USDC in coordination with law enforcement. Former Binance CEO @cz_binance said it “does look like a hack” and that, as a shareholder, he expects user funds to be fully covered.

