Pyth Network now streams US Treasury yields in real time

@PythNetwork has launched live feeds for US government bond yields across seven terms, 2 to 30 years, updated every 200 milliseconds and calculated from Pyth’s Treasury price data. The US Treasury publishes its official curve only once a day, from a 3:30pm New York snapshot.

The feeds run from 2:30am to 5pm New York time on weekdays, so they catch the moves around inflation data and Fed decisions. Pyth ($PYTH) says they can help value tokenized Treasury funds and set fixed rates on lending apps, and short-term bills will follow.

